# Docs: Timestamp Snapshot Files

## Rule

Do not write snapshot/status docs as if they are eternal. **Snapshot docs must have a timestamp in the filename.**

- Use the pattern: `NAME-YYYY-MM-DD.md` (e.g. `REFACTORING-2026-01-28.md`, `NEW_ARCHITECTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS-2026-01-28.md`).
- Apply to: implementation status, refactoring notes, current-state analysis, audit reports, and any doc that is a point-in-time snapshot.
- When updating such a doc, create a **new** dated file (e.g. `REFACTORING-2026-02-15.md`) or overwrite only if you explicitly keep the same date.
- Design/spec docs that are the ongoing source of truth (e.g. FEATURES_AND_REQUIREMENTS_USER_FLOW.md, REDESIGN_ARCHITECTURE_AND_INTENT.md) stay without a date in the filename unless they become snapshots.

## Rationale

Snapshot docs with dates in the name make it clear they are not eternal; readers know when the snapshot was taken and can create new dated files when updating.
